#
# classes.tbl — the class table of omx-rt-gate(1): the external symbols an audio or a worker root
# may call, each with its class, the arm that measured it and the reason. Classification, never a
# waiver: a row names a SYMBOL, never a site, a field, a file or a function of ours (one of ours is
# walked through its graph, never classified). No per-consumer list, no known red, no "cannot
# prove" row. At load a row is REFUSED, and the gate judges nothing (exit 2), when it names
# anything but a symbol, carries a class outside the closed set, has no reason or no arm, repeats
# a symbol, or classifies a forbidden one (forbidden.tbl).
#
#   <symbol> <class> <arm>:<case> <reason>
#
# The classes, a closed set:
#   maths         libm: arithmetic on the arguments, no allocation, no lock. Domain errors set errno
#                 (a thread-local word) and return a value; nothing waits.
#   bulk-memory   memcpy, memmove, memset, memcmp: a bounded pass over caller-owned bytes.
#   word-atomic   an atomic read-modify-write on one machine word, lock-free on the target. At -O0
#                 the compiler emits lock-free atomics inline; a call to a libatomic entry (a wider
#                 or unaligned object, which may take a lock) is no row here and reads red.
#   clock         a clock read: clock_gettime on a vDSO clock, no system call.
#   ftz-register  the floating-point control register (flush to zero, denormals are zero): the
#                 compiler emits these inline (_mm_setcsr, the aarch64 FPCR builtins); a library
#                 call that wraps one would be a row here.
#   wake          a wake that never waits. sem_post is a wake, like FUTEX_WAKE: an atomic increment,
#                 and a futex wake only when a waiter sleeps; it never blocks the caller. sem_wait and
#                 sem_timedwait are not wakes: they stay forbidden (forbidden.tbl, RT-BLOCK).
#
# The arm: externals-arm (tools/rt-gate/externals-arm.c, make rt-gate) calls each symbol over a
# spread of arguments with the process's allocator interposed and requires zero allocations; every
# row's case must be measured there. It cannot see a lock taken inside the library or the time a
# call takes: the class's reason above is what carries those.

sinf maths externals-arm:sinf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
cosf maths externals-arm:cosf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
tanf maths externals-arm:tanf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
tanhf maths externals-arm:tanhf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
expf maths externals-arm:expf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
exp2f maths externals-arm:exp2f libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
logf maths externals-arm:logf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
log2f maths externals-arm:log2f libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
log10f maths externals-arm:log10f libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
sqrtf maths externals-arm:sqrtf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
floorf maths externals-arm:floorf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
ceilf maths externals-arm:ceilf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
powf maths externals-arm:powf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
fminf maths externals-arm:fminf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
fmaxf maths externals-arm:fmaxf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
nextafterf maths externals-arm:nextafterf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
lrintf maths externals-arm:lrintf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
lroundf maths externals-arm:lroundf libm, single precision: arithmetic on the arguments
sin maths externals-arm:sin libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
cos maths externals-arm:cos libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
tan maths externals-arm:tan libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
sinh maths externals-arm:sinh libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
exp maths externals-arm:exp libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
log maths externals-arm:log libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
log2 maths externals-arm:log2 libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
log10 maths externals-arm:log10 libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
sqrt maths externals-arm:sqrt libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
floor maths externals-arm:floor libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
ceil maths externals-arm:ceil libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
pow maths externals-arm:pow libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
hypot maths externals-arm:hypot libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
atan2 maths externals-arm:atan2 libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
fmin maths externals-arm:fmin libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
fmax maths externals-arm:fmax libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
copysign maths externals-arm:copysign libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
lrint maths externals-arm:lrint libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
llround maths externals-arm:llround libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
lround maths externals-arm:lround libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments
ldexp maths externals-arm:ldexp libm, double precision: arithmetic on the arguments

memcpy bulk-memory externals-arm:memcpy a bounded pass over caller-owned bytes
memmove bulk-memory externals-arm:memmove a bounded pass over caller-owned bytes
memset bulk-memory externals-arm:memset a bounded pass over caller-owned bytes
memcmp bulk-memory externals-arm:memcmp a bounded pass over caller-owned bytes

clock_gettime clock externals-arm:clock_gettime CLOCK_MONOTONIC through the vDSO: no system call

sem_post wake externals-arm:sem_post an atomic increment; a futex wake only when a waiter sleeps
